{"data":{"target":{"id":"ENSG00000072849","approvedSymbol":"DERL2","functionDescriptions":["Functional component of endoplasmic reticulum-associated degradation (ERAD) for misfolded lumenal glycoproteins, but not that of misfolded nonglycoproteins. May act by forming a channel that allows the retrotranslocation of misfolded glycoproteins into the cytosol where they are ubiquitinated and degraded by the proteasome. May mediate the interaction between VCP and misfolded glycoproteins (PubMed:16186509, PubMed:16449189). May also be involved in endoplasmic reticulum stress-induced pre-emptive quality control, a mechanism that selectively attenuates the translocation of newly synthesized proteins into the endoplasmic reticulum and reroutes them to the cytosol for proteasomal degradation (PubMed:26565908). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16186509, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16449189, ECO:0000269|PubMed:26565908}.","(Microbial infection) In contrast to DERL1, it is not involved in the degradation of MHC class I heavy chains following infection by cytomegaloviruses. ."],"proteinIds":[{"id":"Q9GZP9","source":"uniprot_swissprot"},{"id":"I3L0R8","source":"uniprot_trembl"},{"id":"I3L1S8","source":"uniprot_trembl"},{"id":"I3L1T3","source":"uniprot_trembl"},{"id":"I3L1W3","source":"uniprot_trembl"},{"id":"I3L3R8","source":"uniprot_trembl"},{"id":"I3L4W7","source":"uniprot_trembl"},{"id":"K7EQE8","source":"uniprot_trembl"},{"id":"ENSP00000158771","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000458296","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000458448","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000459072","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000459083","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000459154","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000460671","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000461603","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000467794","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000559637","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000559638","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00000559639","source":"ensembl_PRO"},{"id":"ENSP00